    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158-a3">

                <pb facs="0326" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg210"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Diplomatic Circular No. 66.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">loan and indemnity payments.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The Dean has the honour to submit, herewith, for the approval of his honourable
                    colleagues a draft reply which he has prepared to the Wai Chiao Pu note of the
                    9th ultimo relative to the procedure for meeting the service of loan and
                    indemnity payments from Customs funds.</p>
                <p>The draft reply contains the reservation suggested by his excellency the Russian
                    Minister and endorsed by his excellency the Italian Minister in the observations
                    they were good enough to offer on the Décanat Circular No. 57 of June 14th.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
